In article <1993Aug18.092528.10328@praxis.co.uk>, bjb@praxis.co.uk (Ben Bell) writes:
> Is there an easy way to tell whether a 'd' is your dog or a Jackal
> etc. I mean, is there an option that allows you to make it look
> different on screen when it's tame? I know that you can look at it and
> it Hack will tell you that it's tame but it would be nice to be able
> to change it's colour or invert it on a mono system or something.
> 
If you just want to know your pet from other monsters - enable 
hilite_pet option. You may also try setting color - if yuor executable
has ben compiled with textcolor enabled, you'll see different mosters
in different colours (dogs will be white - while jackals, wolves, etc
will be yellow or brown). This way however you'll not be able to tell
your pet from other dogs (hilite_pet does not work when color is
enabled)...

